    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/4/74080.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 79,
    "turn_text": "Well, you and I agree. I mean, that was a real deterrent for me. Now, I generally speaking, wasn't a mischievous person anyway. But there is no way I was going to take a chance of my father with his gigantic hands tattooing my rear end if I decided to act like an idiot. I mean, it was very weird that I got myself in trouble. You could ask my mom this. Because I was afraid. First of all, I wanted to impress him. I wanted to impress her too. And secondly, I didn't want to be the bad kid. I had two older sisters. They were the bad kids. But for me, I was not going to have my father's wrath because I did something stupid. And I talked back to him here and there. And I got his wrath here and there anyway. But I wasn't the guy that would go and take over an $8 million mansion and hold a house party and not worry about the ramifications.",
