    "turn_text": "yes. So we were looking at this going, what on earth is stopping you from taking two more feet forward and opening it, they didn't try the door. How is that possible? Because the story that we got at first was that they needed to track down the janitor. The janitor had the keys, and then the story we just had a couple of days ago was, well, they didn't have a specific key to that door, so they were trying the master key on other doors to see if they could find the actual master before going into that door. They weren't even trying the actual door where the guy was. where he was killing people. And Aradondo gets worn in a week later into the city council, and he still has his job? I don't know this guy. Might be a nice guy. I'm not here to say he's a horrible person. I'll say this, dereliction of duty. I'll say this, horrible decisions that were made, he should not benefit from any taxpayer's dime after that display of cowardice. And how do you not try the door? I just don't understand, I want to understand it. I want to say, okay, I get it now. They didn't try the door because. And for the days after the actual massacre in Uvaldi, we were hearing, though, you're going to hear some information that shows why police did what they did. That never came out. That never showed up. They never came to fruition. And I think there were good cops in the hallway that were listening to Arendondo, Arendondo, and probably shouldn't have been. And this is, I mean, as this thing unfolds and more information is coming in a month later, we're finding out even worse than we thought. which is crazy to me. I'm glad that he's on leave of absence. He should be launched from that job. Goodbye. If you're the chief of police of the ISD and 2021 innocent people died on your watch, maybe you shouldn't have that job and certainly shouldn't be on the city council. So that's going to be interesting to watch that as well. Is there anything else that's popped up on this? Cause I mean, it seems like every day there's more information",
